{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-59926",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $6:24$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{24}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($6$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($24$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $2,$ we divide the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6÷3}{24÷3}=\\frac{2}{8}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $16,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of the previous fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 2}{8\\times 2}=\\frac{4}{16}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $16$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $8$ and $4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-59926\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>We start with the ratio <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"137\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>6</mn></mstyle></mrow><mo>:</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>24</mn></mstyle></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and write it as a fraction:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"138\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"block\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>6</mn></mstyle></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>24</mn></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>So the numerator represents the left-hand entry (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"139\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>6</mn></mstyle></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"140\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mn>24</mn></mstyle></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>).</p>\n<p>We can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>To create a numerator of <mjx-containe